hello i'm darren pemberton  deputy leader of stratfor navy district  council and lead member for planning  policy  we are consulting on a site allocations  plan and one of the specific proposals  in chapter seven  proposal rural four at me unveil known  locally as me and vale woodland  has already arised considerable public  interest  so i just wanted to take the opportunity  to set out while we are consulting on  this proposal  with a little of the history of the  wider site  the site is part of the wider me and  vale community being developed on the  former long marston engineer resources  depot  in planning terms it was accepted some  time ago as a previously developed or  brownfield  site the wider depot site is included  within  development policy as11  large rural brownfield sites  of the stratford-upon-avon core strategy  adopted in 2016.  this definition for the site is entirely  consistent with the government's  own definition of brownfield land set  out in the national planning policy  framework or  mppf the original plans for the  moonville community  also included development on part of the  me and vale woodland site in question  as part of a leisure park that  ultimately has never come forward  this site was also consulted on last  year in an earlier version of the site  allocations plan  as a reserve housing site it is no  longer needed for that purpose  but it is important to define its future  in planning terms  and has now been included as a  standalone allocation  because of this we feel that it is vital  to consult the public  at this draft stage as to whether the  proposal ruled or for  me and val woodland is appropriate and  should be brought forward  in terms of the proposal that is the  subject of the consultation  it would result in development of part  of the existing plantation woodland  the proposal explicitly acknowledges  this and seeks to balance the loss of  trees by retaining the mature trees  strengthening biodiversity across the  site  and maintaining and enhancing public  access  the figure of 300 homes specified is set  out as an absolute maximum  any development will also need to ensure  that it does not undermine the  operations of the adjacent  rail technology center which we are  seeking to safeguard for inward  investment  as the home of zero carbon train  development  under proposal rural three  the proposal also requires that the  developer will work with the local  community  in terms of this proposal the land in  question is not currently protected by  any tree preservation order  nor is it designated as a wildlife site  it is however part of a wider area of  land warwickshire county council are  considering for a potential wildlife  site  but have not yet progressed the district  council is in discussion with them to  conduct the appropriate surveys  to establish the ecological value of the  site  since the pandemic struck the value of  the amenity of the woodlands for  residents of me and vale and beyond  has increased immensely since the  publication of the site allocation plan  proposals  there has been widespread and strong  feeling expressed  that the site should be preserved  entirely as woodland with enhanced  biodiversity  to create a green lung for the growing  myeonvale community  this is an entirely plausible potential  approach for the site that sees an  entirely different future for me and  vale woodland  so what we really need in order to  consider the best future for the site  is for as many of you as possible to let  us have your comments on the proposal  before you  and if you do not favor it what exactly  you would like to see the site look like  in future  together with any specific ideas that  you may have about what that looks like  i would reiterate that this is your  opportunity to have your say  and this council does listen and take  seriously the results of public  consultation in all its decision making  processes  so please do send in your comments and  thoughts on the site  details of how to respond to the  consultation can be found at our website  www.stratfor.gov  dot uk forward slash s-a-p-p-o  and the consultation runs until 5 pm on  the 18th of december 2020  i look forward to seeing your  representations  and thank you for your participation
 

